  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "33 total worker jobs: 31 core + 2 required packages",
      "items": [
        "Source snapshot b3ccf5d160d9f8bfdffbc1820f776737f4077eef. Click nodes for pinned source evidence. Default select creates 16 independent answers, then 15 independent judgments across four fixed rounds. Both finalists require package jobs: 33 total, or 34 with a blind baseline judge. Retries add jobs.",
        "Fresh workers get exactly their generated brief; disable inherited history. Keep strategy cards and other judgments away from judges. The coordinator never competes, revises entries, judges, or chooses a winner.",
        "Wave size defaults to 1. Confirm capacity and subtract the coordinator and other active work; four total slots allow at most three available workers. Wait for completion, check files and release worker slots when required."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Unchanged answers, usable finalist guides",
      "items": [
        "Hash every completed original before the first judge prompts. Prompt generation, collect, advance, view and winner reporting verify frozen originals. Missing or changed bytes block progress: restore originals instead of re-freezing altered answers. Fixed branches carry winners forward unchanged.",
        "After the champion and optional blind baseline result, run artifacts for BOTH final-round entrants. Each package contains implementation.md, candidate.json, a real diagram.html and its Archify finalize summary. The guides explain unchanged recommendations; they do not revise entries. There is no optional diagram fallback.",
        "accept-artifact validates canonical paths, original-answer and package hashes, receipt bindings, and validate/deliver/check/browser-check passes. The coordinator records acceptance; workers must not invent receipts or write acceptance manifests.",
        "Only one coordinator changes arena.json; use the explicit absolute RUN for commands. Worker file boundaries are prompt rules rather than an OS sandbox. Applying a proposed project diff remains a separate user decision."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Every answer stays accessible; completion is gated",
      "items": [
        "The required Arena results viewer makes every original answer selectable from the list and bracket, with judge reasons and scores. Both finalists have Answer, Implementation and Archify tabs. Assumptions and review scope remain present in collapsed sections. Technical run details are collapsed below the plain Arena results header.",
        "Export inside RUN/viewer or RUN/visual, protecting originals and state. Refresh after each wave, round and accepted package. A current viewer fingerprint, readable originals, current copied diagrams and both accepted packages are required before next reports DONE and winner can deliver.",
        "Strict collect checks numeric scores, boolean fatal flags, standing lists and match identity; invalid verdicts are quarantined. Ordinary jobs have two total attempts; match/final judges have three. Keep attempt counts under RUN. Missing, unreadable, invalid or stale required outputs block completion; after limits stop incomplete with the failed job and resumable RUN.",
        "If the blind baseline wins, report it as the preferred answer alongside the tournament result. Return the full selected answer, decisive reasons, counts and record location, and link the required viewer and both packages."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Validation limits and explicit optional evolve mode",
      "items": [
        "Successful Archify artifact/browser checks validate diagram generation and provenance, not the semantic accuracy of a recommendation or guide. Review meaning against the original answer and source, marking proposed steps honestly. A bracket winner is not proof of correctness.",
        "Only explicit --mode evolve adds two attack jobs, two defense/revision jobs and one judge per match: 91 core jobs + two required packages = 93 total, or 94 with baseline. This optional mode is outside the main path. Historical saved runs retain their historical mode/delivery rules.",
        "For a one-entry run, require one finalist package. The diagram shows the default 16-entry run."
      ]
    }
  ]
